        "title": "Stimulant Crops - Coffee, Tea, and Cacao",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The three great stimulant crops — coffee, tea, and cacao — share one important characteristic: they were all considered luxury goods or medicines before they became everyday commodities, and all three changed the intellectual and social life of the civilizations that adopted them. Coffee houses preceded the Enlightenment. Tea became a geopolitical flashpoint. Cacao was sacred currency."
